{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1422","published":"2026-11-23T20:01:46.351Z","modified":"2026-11-23T20:15:03.561089816Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-53790","EUVD-2026-58098"],"details":"rsync before 3.5.0 contains multiple command and argument injection vulnerabilities that allow attackers to execute arbitrary commands by supplying malicious input through several code paths, including the `RSYNC_CONNECT_PROG` environment variable, daemon hooks, the rsync-ssl wrapper, and remote-shell command newline injection. Attackers can inject shell metacharacters or newline characters into unsanitized user-supplied values such as hostnames and hostspecs to execute arbitrary commands under the privileges of the rsync process or the invoking user.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/rsync_jll?uuid=191d6b87-264a-55f5-a0e2-c8fbce9a1ce0"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.5.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1422.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/releases/tag/v3.5.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/security/advisories/GHSA-5hcf-7xxm-rmqq"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rsync-command-injection-via-multiple-code-paths"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"samba:rsync":["< 3.5.0"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53790","id":"CVE-2026-53790","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:04.993Z","modified":"2026-11-06T16:01:25.930Z","published":"2026-08-13T15:19:43.200Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-53790"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-58098","id":"EUVD-2026-58098","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:06.499Z","modified":"2026-08-14T16:50:08Z","published":"2026-0